From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lech Piekarski <isilweo@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 20:34:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: q6asm-dai: check the capture buffer queueing in
 prepare

For capture, q6asm_dai_prepare() queues the read buffers right after
sending the encoder configuration, before checking whether that
command succeeded, and ignores the result of q6asm_read(). A stream
whose configuration was rejected thus gets read commands, and a stream
that could queue only some of its buffers is reported as prepared.

Queue the buffers only once the configuration has succeeded, and undo
the setup if a buffer cannot be queued.

Fixes: 2a9e92d371db ("ASoC: qdsp6: q6asm: Add q6asm dai driver")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Assisted-by: Codex:gpt-6.2-astra
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Source: https://github.com/isilweo/linux/commit/cfc38d4c15795bbf541c1988f07dca1d11cf2c7a
Base-commit: 1c1a919fd728c881e7ccaf3cf18a3cf3055e0429
---
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm-dai.c | 17 ++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm-dai.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm-dai.c
index 841853a541db..24b750967cf2 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm-dai.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm-dai.c
@@ -329,17 +329,24 @@ static int q6asm_dai_prepare(struct snd_soc_component *component,
 							   runtime->rate,
 							   runtime->channels,
 							   prtd->bits_per_sample);
-
-		/* Queue the buffers */
-		for (i = 0; i < runtime->periods; i++)
-			q6asm_read(prtd->audio_client, prtd->stream_id);
-
 	}
 	if (ret < 0) {
 		dev_err(dev, "%s: CMD Format block failed\n", __func__);
 		goto err;
 	}
 
+	if (substream->stream == SNDRV_PCM_STREAM_CAPTURE) {
+		/* Queue the buffers */
+		for (i = 0; i < runtime->periods; i++) {
+			ret = q6asm_read(prtd->audio_client, prtd->stream_id);
+			if (ret < 0) {
+				dev_err(dev, "%s: queuing capture buffer %d failed: %d\n",
+					__func__, i, ret);
+				goto err;
+			}
+		}
+	}
+
 	prtd->state = Q6ASM_STREAM_RUNNING;
 	return 0;
 
